## 5. Key Features & Implementation

### 5.1 Physics Engine (Matter.js)

The core of the application is a fully interactive 2D physics engine:

- **Body Types:** Circles, rectangles, and polygons with configurable mass, density, friction, restitution, and air friction
- **Constraint Types:** Ropes (low stiffness), springs (elastic), pivots (fixed rotation points), motors (angular velocity), and welds (rigid connections)
- **Material Presets:** 8 pre-configured materials (Metal, Wood, Rubber, Ice, Stone, Glass, Foam, Custom) with realistic physics properties
- **Collision Detection:** Matter.js SAT (Separating Axis Theorem) for accurate narrow-phase detection
- **Static Bodies:** Supports fixed bodies (ramps, anchors) via `Body.setStatic()` after creation

![Main Canvas](C:/Users/lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/brain/62fa5e5d-fbed-4588-ba64-ed3337f8de5e/report_images/main_canvas.png)

### 5.2 Experiment Library

8 pre-built experiments stored as serialized Matter.js world snapshots:

| # | Experiment | Difficulty | Physics Concepts |
|---|-----------|-----------|-----------------|
| 1 | Simple Pendulum | Beginner | Oscillation, gravity, energy |
| 2 | Newton's Cradle | Intermediate | Momentum, collision, energy transfer |
| 3 | Inclined Plane | Beginner | Friction, gravity, forces |
| 4 | Spring-Mass System | Beginner | Oscillation, spring, harmonic motion |
| 5 | Projectile Motion | Beginner | Trajectory, velocity, gravity |
| 6 | Domino Chain | Intermediate | Chain-reaction, momentum, rotation |
| 7 | Rope Bridge | Advanced | Constraints, tension, load |
| 8 | Atwood Machine | Intermediate | Pulley, tension, net force |

![Experiment Library](C:/Users/lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/brain/62fa5e5d-fbed-4588-ba64-ed3337f8de5e/report_images/experiment_gallery.png)

### 5.3 World Serialization / Deserialization

A custom serializer (`physicsSerializer.js`) converts the live Matter.js world into a portable JSON snapshot format:

```js
// Serialization schema (Version 1)
{
  version: 1,
  timestamp: Date.now(),
  gravity: { x: 0, y: 1 },
  bodies: [
    {
      id, type, label, position, angle, velocity,
      circleRadius, width, height,
      mass, density, friction, frictionAir, restitution,
      isStatic, isSensor, render: { fillStyle, strokeStyle, lineWidth }
    }
  ],
  constraints: [
    {
      id, label, bodyAId, bodyBId,
      pointA, pointB, length, stiffness, damping,
      render: { strokeStyle, lineWidth }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Key design decisions:**
- `bodyAId: null` with `pointA` as a world coordinate creates a **fixed-point anchor** (used in pendulums)
- `Body.setStatic(body, true)` is called **after** `Body.setAngle()` to ensure static bodies (ramps) are correctly initialized
- A `BOUNDARY_LABELS` set (`Ground`, `Wall-L`, `Wall-R`) ensures environment bodies are never serialized or removed

### 5.4 Real-Time Collaboration

The multiplayer system uses a **host-authoritative** sync model over Socket.io:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Host
    participant Server
    participant Guest

    Host->>Server: room:join (create room)
    Server->>Host: room:joined (isHost: true)
    
    Guest->>Server: room:join (join existing)
    Server->>Guest: room:joined (worldState)
    Server->>Host: room:user-joined
    
    loop Every 1 second
        Host->>Server: world:sync (serialized world)
        Server->>Guest: world:synced (serialized world)
    end
    
    Host->>Server: sim:toggle (play/pause)
    Server->>Guest: sim:toggled
    
    Host->>Server: experiment:load (snapshot)
    Server->>Guest: experiment:loaded (snapshot)
```

![Collaboration Modal](C:/Users/lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/brain/62fa5e5d-fbed-4588-ba64-ed3337f8de5e/report_images/collaboration_modal.png)

**Socket Events:**

| Event | Direction | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| `room:join` | Client → Server | Create or join a room |
| `room:joined` | Server → Client | Confirm join + send user list |
| `world:sync` | Host → Server → Guests | Full world state broadcast (1s interval) |
| `sim:toggle` | Any → Server → Others | Play/Pause state sync |
| `experiment:load` | Any → Server → Others | Template experiment broadcast |
| `cursor:move` | Any → Server → Others | Live cursor position |
| `physics:delta` | Any → Server → Others | Incremental physics updates |

### 5.5 Live Analytics Dashboard

The `useAnalytics` hook samples the physics engine state at configurable intervals and renders three live charts:

1. **Velocity** (px/frame) — RMS velocity of all dynamic bodies
2. **Kinetic Energy** (J) — Total ½mv² across all bodies
3. **Net Force** (N) — Sum of all force magnitudes

Additionally, a **Collision Log** tab captures every collision event with body labels, relative velocity, and timestamp.

### 5.6 Property Inspector

When a body is selected on the canvas, the right-side Inspector panel displays and allows editing of:

- **Label** — Custom name for the body
- **Material** — Quick-select from 8 presets
- **Mass, Friction, Bounce (Restitution), Density** — Fine-grained physics tuning
- **Color** — Custom render fill color
- **Static toggle** — Lock/unlock body position

